  ($qb$S07C07Q09$qb$, $qb$S07$qb$, $qb$C07$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The board and senior leadership team actively monitor the organisation's capability pipeline for future readiness:$qb$, $qb$Yes — capability readiness is a board-level agenda item with regular reviews$qb$, $qb$Partially — some monitoring occurs at senior leadership level$qb$, $qb$Rarely — capability readiness is reviewed occasionally but not as a systematic governance item$qb$, $qb$No — capability pipeline monitoring is not a governance priority$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S07C07Q10$qb$, $qb$S07$qb$, $qb$C07$qb$, $qb$L+MM+E$qb$, $qb$The overall learning agility of your organisation — its ability to learn and adapt faster than the environment changes — is:$qb$, $qb$High — the organisation learns and adapts with speed; this is a competitive advantage$qb$, $qb$Moderate — adaptation is adequate for current conditions$qb$, $qb$Low — the organisation adapts slowly and is periodically caught off-guard by environmental change$qb$, $qb$Very low — learning agility is a critical organisational weakness$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
