  ($qb$S20C08Q05$qb$, $qb$S20$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The lessons from previous transformation attempts that are being applied this time in your organisation are:$qb$, $qb$Explicitly identified and built into the current transformation design$qb$, $qb$Generally known and informally applied$qb$, $qb$Partially known — some lessons are being applied but others have not been captured$qb$, $qb$Not captured — the organisation is not formally applying lessons from past transformation experience$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S20C08Q06$qb$, $qb$S20$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L+MM$qb$, $qb$The degree to which employees trust that this transformation will be different from previous attempts in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$High — employees have confidence in the current leadership and approach$qb$, $qb$Moderate — most employees are cautiously hopeful$qb$, $qb$Low — employee scepticism from past experience is significant$qb$, $qb$Very low — employee cynicism about transformation is deep and would significantly impede progress$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S20C08Q07$qb$, $qb$S20$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The quality of data available about what worked and did not work in previous transformations in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Excellent — comprehensive transformation retrospective data is available$qb$, $qb$Generally adequate — useful data on past transformation is available$qb$, $qb$Limited — some data exists but it is incomplete$qb$, $qb$Non-existent — no structured data on previous transformation outcomes is available$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S20C08Q08$qb$, $qb$S20$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The degree to which the organisation has built internal transformation capability from previous experiences in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Significantly — previous transformations have built genuine internal change management expertise$qb$, $qb$Somewhat — some capability has been built$qb$, $qb$Minimally — limited capability was retained after previous transformations$qb$, $qb$Not at all — the organisation starts fresh each time without accumulated transformation capability$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S20C08Q09$qb$, $qb$S20$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The resilience of the organisation in bouncing back from transformation setbacks in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$High — the organisation learns and recovers quickly when transformation hits obstacles$qb$, $qb$Generally adequate — the organisation manages setbacks without losing momentum$qb$, $qb$Limited — setbacks tend to significantly slow or derail transformation momentum$qb$, $qb$Very limited — the organisation has a poor track record of recovering from transformation setbacks$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S20C08Q10$qb$, $qb$S20$qb$, $qb$C08$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$Overall, the relevance of previous transformation experience to the current effort in your organisation:$qb$, $qb$Is a significant asset — experience has built confidence, capability, and institutional knowledge$qb$, $qb$Is a useful foundation — past experience provides helpful context$qb$, $qb$Is limited — past experience is not highly relevant to the current transformation$qb$, $qb$Is a liability — poor past experience is creating headwinds for the current effort$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S20C09Q01$qb$, $qb$S20$qb$, $qb$C09$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The degree of alignment among board members on the need for and direction of transformation in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Strong — the board is unified in its support for transformation$qb$, $qb$Generally aligned — most board members are supportive$qb$, $qb$Mixed — some board members are strongly supportive; others are sceptical$qb$, $qb$Misaligned — significant board-level disagreement about transformation is a risk$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
  ($qb$S20C09Q02$qb$, $qb$S20$qb$, $qb$C09$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$Alignment between the CEO and the next level of leadership on transformation in your organisation is:$qb$, $qb$Strong — the CEO and direct reports are fully aligned on the transformation agenda$qb$, $qb$Generally aligned — most executives are aligned$qb$, $qb$Partially aligned — some executives are aligned; others are resistant or uncertain$qb$, $qb$Misaligned — significant misalignment between the CEO and the executive team is a transformation risk$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
