  ($qb$S20C10Q01$qb$, $qb$S20$qb$, $qb$C10$qb$, $qb$L$qb$, $qb$The degree to which the organisation's leadership is specifically interested in a human-centred transformation approach (balancing people and performance) is:$qb$, $qb$Very high — leadership explicitly values and seeks a human-centred approach to transformation$qb$, $qb$High — leadership believes that people and performance must go hand in hand$qb$, $qb$Moderate — leadership acknowledges the people dimension but is primarily performance-focused$qb$, $qb$Low — leadership is primarily focused on financial and operational outcomes without strong emphasis on the people dimension$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, true),
